{"kind":"snippet","id":"trace-ledger","repo":"AnwarDebes/trace","ref":"cc3a1a432ab010f58758f55caeec51d853086573","path":"tracekit/ledger.py","lang":"python","startLine":1,"lines":[
[["\"\"\"","str"],["Tamper-evident certificate ledger for agent sessions.","com"]],
[],
[["Every decision TRACE makes (a content verdict, a behaviour step) is appended","com"]],
[["to a hash-chained, HMAC-signed ledger.  The construction follows the","com"]],
[["tamper-evident logging line of work (Schneier & Kelsey, 1999; Crosby & Wallach,","com"]],
[["2009) and Certificate Transparency (RFC 6962):","com"]],
[],
[["    entry_hash[i] = SHA256( entry_hash[i-1] || canonical(payload[i]) )","com"]],
[["    signature[i]  = HMAC-SHA256( key, entry_hash[i] )","com"]],
[],
[["and the whole session is summarised by a binary Merkle root over the entry","com"]],
[["hashes, signed once.  The resulting :class:`SessionCertificate` is small,","com"]],
[["self-contained, and, crucially, **independently verifiable without the","com"]],
[["model**: an auditor holding the shared secret key (HMAC is symmetric, so the","com"]],
[["verification key *is* the signing key: this gives authentication, not","com"]],
[["non-repudiation) can","com"]],
[],
[["  1. recompute the hash chain and detect any modified / inserted / deleted /","com"]],
[["     reordered entry (the chain or the Merkle root breaks);","com"]],
[["  2. re-evaluate every content CNF receipt (AND of included literal values);","com"]],
[["  3. replay the recorded event stream through the policy monitors and confirm","com"]],
[["     the recorded verdict matches.","com"]],
[],
[["Because each receipt is self-contained and signed, *later* online updates to the","com"]],
[["guard cannot retroactively invalidate a sealed certificate.  This is the bridge","com"]],
[["from a one-shot decision to a verifiable session-level audit trail required by,","com"]],
[["e.g., EU AI Act Article 12 (record-keeping) and Article 26 (deployer logs).","com"]],
[["\"\"\"","str"]],
[],
